  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.47 Navigable frontage",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.47 “Navigable frontage” means, for non-tidal waters, the frontage that can be accessed by a boat having at least a 6-foot beam and 2-foot draft at normal high water.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.45)",
